ame": "Uzbek"}, "word": "axborot"}, {"language": {"code": "uz", "name": "Uzbek"}, "word": "informatsiya"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "thông tin"}, {"language": {"code": "cy", "name": "Welsh"}, "word": "gwybodaeth"}, {"language": {"code": "cy", "name": "Welsh"}, "word": "hysbysrwydd"}, {"language": {"code": "yi", "name": "Yiddish"}, "word": "אינפֿאָרמאַציע"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "The act of informing or imparting knowledge; notification.", "tags": ["uncountable", "usually"], "examples": ["For your information, I did this because I wanted to."], "quotes": [{"text": "At this time a great uneasiness became manifest among the Castilians, and it was rumored that Magallanes was going to deliver them over to the Portuguese; and they resolved to mutiny and seize the ships. Magallanes upon obtaining information of this was sorely grieved. He summoned the guilty ones before him one by one, but they flatly refused to come.", "reference": "1903–1909, “Extracto de una carta (Extract of a letter from the Indies)”, in Emma Helen Blair, James Alexander Robertson, editors, The Philippine Islands, 1493–1898, volume 1, pages 297-299:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "gur", "name": "Farefare"}, "word": "ko'osgo"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tiedonanto"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tiedotus"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tiedottaminen"}, {"language": {"code": "gl", "name": "Galician"}, "word": "información"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "tájékoztatás"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "felvilágosítás"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "informálás"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "értesítés"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "közlés"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "hírközlés"}, {"language": {"code": "enm", "name": "Middle English"}, "word": "enformacioun"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(law, countable) A statement of criminal activity brought before a judge or magistrate; in the UK, used to inform a magistrate of an offence and request a warrant; in the US, an accusation brought before a judge without a grand jury indictment.", "tags": ["countable", "usually"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "That friend, […] added, with a smile, that he had more than once amused himself with the thought of a verbarian Attorney-General, authorized to bring informations ex officio against the writer or editor of any work in extensive circulation, who, after due notice issued, should persevere in misusing a word.", "reference": "1830, S[amuel] T[aylor] Coleridge, “Concerning the Right Idea of the Constitution”, in On the Constitution of the Church and State, according to the Idea of Each: […], London: Hurst, Chance, and Co., →OCLC, footnote *, page 19:"}, {"text": "'We have another deposition, doctor, to take; Mr. Irons, here, is prepared to swear informations of very singular importance.'", "reference": "1863, J[oseph] Sheridan Le Fanu, The House by the Church-yard. […], volume (please specify |volume=I to III), London: Tinsley, Brothers, […], →OCLC:"}, {"text": "On May 21, 1792, the Attorney General filed an information against Paine charging him with seditious libel.", "reference": "1968, Carl B. Cone, The English Jacobins, New York: Charles Scribner's Sons, page 131:"}, {"text": "The second formal method of charging someone with a crime is by information. Informations are filed by prosecutors without grand jury review.", "reference": "2011, Daniel E. Hall, Criminal Law and Procedure:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) The act of informing against someone, passing on incriminating knowledge; accusation.", "tags": ["obsolete", "uncountable", "usually"], 